        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix Ollama incomplete stream model fallback",
        "body": "Closes #100460.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nWhen Ollama closes a native NDJSON stream before its required final response, the stream adapter emits a deterministic provider error. That error was not classified at the Ollama provider boundary, so the normal model-fallback loop could not advance to the next configured candidate.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe final fix keeps provider-specific behavior in the Ollama plugin instead of adding an Ollama literal to the generic agent loop. Both `ollama` and `ollama-cloud` registrations now share one classifier: existing context-window patterns still map to `context_overflow`, while the exact incomplete-stream runtime error maps to `server_error`.\n\nThe producer and classifier share one exported constant, preventing message drift. Unrelated Ollama errors remain unclassified.\n\n## User Impact\n\nA prematurely closed Ollama stream can now advance through configured model fallbacks instead of repeatedly failing the same candidate and ending with a generic request failure.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Existing issue repro: a mock Ollama `/api/chat` returned one incomplete NDJSON chunk and closed; before the fix OpenClaw retried Ollama and never reached fallback, while after the fix it made one Ollama request and returned the fallback response.\n- `extensions/ollama/index.test.ts` proves exact incomplete-stream classification for both Ollama provider ids, preserves context-overflow behavior, and rejects unrelated errors.\n- `extensions/ollama/src/stream-runtime.test.ts` pins the runtime producer to the shared error contract.\n- Exact-head structured AutoReview on `63ca5ba8f31ea3e5e2f9276463d43e1dc52af5f2`: clean, no actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`: passed.\n- Exact-head hosted CI will be linked after the post-push dispatch selects the changed lanes.\n\nAI assistance: Codex performed maintainer review, owner-boundary refactoring, regression-proof selection, and landing preparation.\n",
